{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01H5oCqinSsFk8WqVswR7U5U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system built for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims:\n\n- **It's a single-folder, local-first task/productivity tool** living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` â€” no OneDrive, no syncing, no database. Plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files) are the source of truth.\n\n- **It ships `anchor_gui.py`** (the declared deliverable): a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`, and reads/writes the markdown files directly via a local API.\n\n- **It manages a full task lifecycle** â€” active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored â€” plus quick-capture inbox, per-domain views (academic/commercial/family/writing), and an auto-generated static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It has a CLI mirror (`anchor.py`)** with the same logic/format (done, cancel, save, restore, add, capture, dashboard) and a read-only `rnd` inspection subcommand set.\n\n- **Its main evolution is an \"R&D control surface\"** layered through v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4 (\"Project Cockpit\"), turning each project into a calm single-screen cockpit for **trio-driven R&D** (Researchâ†’researchPrime Â· Planningâ†’Crucible Â· Buildâ†’Foreman). Each lane shows its most-recent session as a status-lit tile that expands inline into a summary-over-terminal panel.\n\n- **It runs real interactive terminal sessions server-side** over Windows ConPTY (`pty_manager.py` + xterm.js, WebSocket/SSE transport), each isolated in its own git worktree, with a durable session registry, engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), cached validated summaries, stage handoffs, and ephemeral deliverable previews (always on a port â‰  8777).\n\n- **It enforces a strict stdlib-only rule with exactly one declared exception** (`pywinpty` for the terminal subsystem, lazy-imported in `pty_manager.py` only; degrades gracefully if absent) â€” verified by `distro.py`'s import scan.\n\n- **It self-tests daily** via `anchor_healthcheck.py` (5 AM Task Scheduler), which fully stubs every model call and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces, writing dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **It's branded** as a Ghost World Labs tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\"\n\nThese claims come straight from the project's `CLAUDE.md`, the locked North Star/decision anchors, and the declared deliverable â€” not inferred."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b650d5c5-3565-4890-989c-c425bf814737","uuid":"2f7608ba-ef3e-49f0-985c-63460a270587","request_id":"req_011Cc1hvXVep3hDEY9bFco9c"}
